sis: epidemiology, pathophysiology, and management.</article-title><source>Clin Microbiol Rev</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>383</fpage><lpage>416</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15831829</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000364-Currie2"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Currie</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fisher</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Howard</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Burrow</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name><name><surname>Selvanayagam</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>The epidemiology of melioidosis in Australia and Papua New Guinea.</article-title><source>Acta Trop</source><volume>74</volume><fpage>121</fpage><lpage>127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10674639</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000364-Dance2"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dance</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Melioidosis as an emerging global problem.</article-title><source>Acta Trop</source><volume>74</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>119</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10674638</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000364-Currie3"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Currie</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Advances and remaining uncertainties in the epidemiology of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic> and melioidosis.</article-title><source>Transactions of the Royal Society of Tropical Medicine and Hygiene</source><volume>102</volume><fpage>225</fpage><lpage>227</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18166205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000364-Inglis1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Inglis</surname><given-names>TJJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rolim</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>De Queiroz Sousa Anas</surname></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Melioidosis in the Americas.</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>75</volume><fpage>947</fpage><lpage>954</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17123994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000364-Tong1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tong</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>He</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Laboratory investigation of ecological factors influencing the environmental presence of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic>.</article-title><source>Microbiol Immunol</source><volume>40</volume><fpage>451</fpage><lpage>453</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8839431</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000364-Chen1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>YS</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kao</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>YL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Effects of soil pH, temperature and water content on the growth of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic>.</article-title><source>Folia Microbiol (Praha)</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>256</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12800512</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000364-Thomas1"><label>13</label><citation ci